Wait: floor is drawn after backdrop and before walls. The wall cache is transparent except walls. drawImage full canvas with transparency. Good.

But cached walls are drawn after floor, same as before. The banner draw after wall cache. Good.

Cache uses default alpha canvas. Fine.

Now adaptive DPR. In frame():
```
const raw = ...
```
Need capture frame duration before overwriting. `const elapsed = now - lastFrame` currently computed. Add perf monitor. Only when playing and document visible and not title/end maybe.

Insert after raw compute:
```
if (G.state === 'playing' && !document.hidden) {
  perfAccum += Math.min(120, raw*1000); perfSamples++;
  if (perfSamples >= 150) {
    const avg = perfAccum/perfSamples;
    if (avg > 42 && maxDpr > 1.05) { maxDpr = Math.max(1, maxDpr - .35); resize(); }
    perfAccum=0; perfSamples=0;
  }
}
```
But `raw` is clamped to .05, so avg > 42ms can never trigger! Use actual elapsed = now-lastFrame before clamp, stored. Need:
```
const elapsed = Math.max(0, now-lastFrame);
const raw = Math.min(.05, elapsed/1000);
```
Then monitor elapsed. Add. Avoid monitor if QS res? Even with res, maxDpr applies but RENDER_SCALE fixed; could still reduce. Fine. But in tests, the low FPS will trigger maxDpr reduction only if devicePixelRatio>1; desktop DPR 1 no change. Mobile screenshot context DPR2: after 150 frames at ~1fps (150s) won't trigger within test. Fine.

Be careful resize() is expensive and called from frame; acceptable at most 3 times. Reset counters after.

Also note first frame elapsed might be huge due init; 150 frames average mostly normal.

Implement.

